API-10: recompute a conduit's slope when a node invert or link offset is set

setNodeValue() and setLinkValue() accepted swmm_NODE_ELEV, swmm_LINK_OFFSET1
and swmm_LINK_OFFSET2 between swmm_open() and swmm_start() but only stored
them. The conduit slope, beta, qFull, qMax and the lengthened length are
computed once, in conduit_validate() during swmm_open(), so the edit had no
effect on LINK_SLOPE, LINK_FULLFLOW or kinematic-wave routing.

The part of conduit_validate() that starts at "compute conduit slope" is
split off unchanged into link_updateSlope(j), which conduit_validate() calls
and the three setters call for the affected conduits (all conduits ending at
the node for NODE_ELEV). It also resets modLength before the lengthening
step, so that a second call does not keep a stale lengthened length. Input
files run as before.

Requires: API-01

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply API-10_swmm530.patch

